<title>USA: General Scanning options to start trading Aug 7.</title>
<headline>General Scanning options to start trading Aug 7.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pacific Exchange (PCX) said Monday it will list options on General Scanning Inc on August 7.</p>
<p>In addition, the Philadelphia Stock Exchange (PHLX) said it would start trading General Scanning options on the same day, two days later than originally scheduled.</p>
<p>The PCX said the options will have strike prices of 15, 17-1/2 and 20 and expirations in September, October, January and April.  Position limits have been set at 4,500 contracts.</p>
<p>The options have been allocated to lead market makers David Post and Joseph Hruban.</p>
<p>((--Chicago derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
